1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,204
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:05,504
Basil hangs his bar magnet on a string, so it can turn

3
00:00:05,524 --> 00:00:06,274
freely.

4
00:00:06,554 --> 00:00:08,304
He spins it again and again.

5
00:00:08,584 --> 00:00:09,764
Where does it stop?

6
00:00:09,819 --> 00:00:11,879
One, a different way every time.

7
00:00:13,089 --> 00:00:15,159
Two, the same way every time.

8
00:00:16,635 --> 00:00:18,145
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:20,617 --> 00:00:24,237
Today, we find out where a hanging magnet stops, and why!

10
00:00:24,734 --> 00:00:27,124
A little swallow is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:27,374 --> 00:00:28,614
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:32,077
Swallows swoop low over a field, catching tiny insects.

13
00:00:32,267 --> 00:00:33,677
Look high, and look low!

14
00:00:33,724 --> 00:00:35,184
You against the Buddies!

15
00:00:35,454 --> 00:00:37,304
Lock in first with your fingers.

16
00:00:37,574 --> 00:00:39,404
One finger for every point.

17
00:00:39,985 --> 00:00:41,285
Today you'll learn:

18
00:00:41,489 --> 00:00:43,499
A freely suspended magnet.

19
00:00:43,695 --> 00:00:45,375
The North-South direction.

20
00:00:45,575 --> 00:00:47,265
Earth is like a magnet.

21
00:00:47,763 --> 00:00:48,703
Are you ready?

22
00:00:49,143 --> 00:00:49,913
Three!

23
00:00:50,293 --> 00:00:50,953
Two!

24
00:00:51,323 --> 00:00:51,973
One!

25
00:00:52,393 --> 00:00:53,113
Go!

26
00:00:54,502 --> 00:00:55,392
Round one!

27
00:00:55,692 --> 00:00:57,582
Where does Basil's magnet stop?

28
00:00:57,862 --> 00:00:59,172
Show me your fingers!

29
00:01:02,643 --> 00:01:03,623
Locked in!

30
00:01:03,751 --> 00:01:04,471
One!

31
00:01:04,621 --> 00:01:07,661
My spinning top falls over a different way every time.

32
00:01:07,761 --> 00:01:09,191
So will the magnet!

33
00:01:09,244 --> 00:01:10,124
Two.

34
00:01:10,354 --> 00:01:12,044
Magnets follow rules.

35
00:01:12,254 --> 00:01:15,014
Unlike poles attract every single time.

36
00:01:15,068 --> 00:01:15,698
Two!

37
00:01:15,858 --> 00:01:17,028
I tried it at home.

38
00:01:17,158 --> 00:01:20,328
The red end always stopped facing my bedroom window!

39
00:01:20,602 --> 00:01:22,062
Be the hanging magnet!

40
00:01:22,342 --> 00:01:23,332
Shrink down.

41
00:01:23,612 --> 00:01:24,542
Quietly.

42
00:01:26,829 --> 00:01:29,439
You are a bar magnet, hanging on a string.

43
00:01:30,239 --> 00:01:32,899
A giant finger spins you round and round!

44
00:01:33,424 --> 00:01:34,494
Slower now.

45
00:01:35,264 --> 00:01:37,664
You swing past a line, and back again.

46
00:01:38,434 --> 00:01:41,114
Something you cannot see turns you gently back.

47
00:01:41,638 --> 00:01:45,018
You stop, with your red end facing the big rain tree.

48
00:01:45,798 --> 00:01:46,978
A spin again!

49
00:01:47,768 --> 00:01:49,178
Slower, and slower.

50
00:01:49,968 --> 00:01:50,928
You stop.

51
00:01:51,748 --> 00:01:53,218
The rain tree again!

52
00:01:54,869 --> 00:01:57,719
The answer is two: the same way every time!

53
00:01:57,979 --> 00:01:59,559
Did you show two fingers?

54
00:01:59,799 --> 00:02:01,198
Put one finger up!

55
00:02:01,218 --> 00:02:04,328
Every time, it comes to rest with its red end facing the

56
00:02:04,348 --> 00:02:05,268
rain tree.

57
00:02:05,558 --> 00:02:07,668
Let's mark the line with two cones!

58
00:02:07,789 --> 00:02:09,299
I think I know why.

59
00:02:09,429 --> 00:02:11,769
The red end faces the goalpost.

60
00:02:11,939 --> 00:02:15,149
Magnets attract steel, so the goalpost turns it.

61
00:02:15,799 --> 00:02:16,949
Look closer.

62
00:02:17,549 --> 00:02:20,995
Hang it in the middle of the field, far from the goalpost.

63
00:02:21,015 --> 00:02:22,555
Hang it in the classroom.

64
00:02:23,135 --> 00:02:26,338
Float it on a plastic lid in a basin of water.

65
00:02:26,358 --> 00:02:29,638
Every time, it comes to rest along the same line.

66
00:02:30,208 --> 00:02:32,193
This line runs North and South.

67
00:02:32,213 --> 00:02:35,883
Freely suspended means hanging so that it can turn freely, such as

68
00:02:35,903 --> 00:02:37,513
a magnet on a string!

69
00:02:38,021 --> 00:02:41,791
The North-South direction means the line from North to South, such as

70
00:02:41,811 --> 00:02:43,741
the line between our cones.

71
00:02:44,071 --> 00:02:47,241
One end faces North, and the other end faces South.

72
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,705
Say it with me!

73
00:02:52,413 --> 00:02:56,523
A freely suspended magnet comes to rest in the North-South direction.

74
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:00,040
My turn!

75
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:03,320
My string got tangled, so I laid the magnet on the bench.

76
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:05,610
Nobody is holding it, so it is free!

77
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:08,070
But it stops a different way every time.

78
00:03:08,194 --> 00:03:09,754
Something is not right.

79
00:03:10,024 --> 00:03:12,204
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

80
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:13,444
Hold on!

81
00:03:18,857 --> 00:03:19,987
Arms crossed?

82
00:03:20,257 --> 00:03:21,467
One finger up!

83
00:03:21,519 --> 00:03:22,389
Watch.

84
00:03:22,579 --> 00:03:25,499
The bench rubs on the magnet and stops it turning.

85
00:03:25,779 --> 00:03:28,219
I hang it up, and it turns freely again!

86
00:03:28,345 --> 00:03:31,413
A freely suspended magnet must be free to turn.

87
00:03:31,433 --> 00:03:32,073
Oops!

88
00:03:32,223 --> 00:03:34,693
Free to turn, not just free from my paws.

89
00:03:34,893 --> 00:03:37,423
But how does the magnet know which way is North?

90
00:03:37,493 --> 00:03:39,080
Nothing is touching it!

91
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:42,590
Maybe a giant magnet is hiding somewhere, turning it round!

92
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,370
Look closer.

93
00:03:44,970 --> 00:03:48,863
Fly up, above Singapore, until you can see the whole Earth.

94
00:03:48,883 --> 00:03:53,003
All over the world, freely suspended magnets come to rest in the

95
00:03:53,023 --> 00:03:54,476
North-South direction.

96
00:03:54,496 --> 00:03:56,146
Basil is nearly right.

97
00:03:56,726 --> 00:04:01,766
Earth behaves like a magnet, with its own North and South poles.

98
00:04:02,291 --> 00:04:05,911
So the Earth turns my magnet round, without even touching it!

99
00:04:08,607 --> 00:04:09,827
Say it with me!

100
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:14,331
Earth behaves like a magnet with its own North and South poles.

101
00:04:14,961 --> 00:04:17,791
It interacts with a freely suspended magnet.

102
00:04:18,381 --> 00:04:22,511
This causes the freely suspended magnet to always point in the North-South

103
00:04:22,531 --> 00:04:23,441
direction.

104
00:04:25,914 --> 00:04:27,374
Show me your score hand!

105
00:04:27,654 --> 00:04:28,684
Two fingers?

106
00:04:28,964 --> 00:04:30,334
You beat the Buddies.

107
00:04:30,614 --> 00:04:31,614
High five!

108
00:04:32,192 --> 00:04:33,622
Did you spot the swallow?

109
00:04:33,912 --> 00:04:35,922
It was on the rim of the netball hoop!

110
00:04:36,047 --> 00:04:37,357
Here is a fun fact!

111
00:04:37,417 --> 00:04:40,547
Every year, swallows fly to Singapore from far away.

112
00:04:40,807 --> 00:04:43,967
Many birds can feel the Earth's magnet, and it helps them find

113
00:04:43,987 --> 00:04:44,847
their way!

114
00:04:44,969 --> 00:04:46,249
Tell someone at home!

115
00:04:46,978 --> 00:04:49,178
Let's read today's key words together!

116
00:04:49,468 --> 00:04:50,228
Ready?

117
00:04:50,515 --> 00:04:51,885
Freely suspended.

118
00:04:53,679 --> 00:04:55,149
North-South direction.

119
00:04:57,084 --> 00:04:58,853
Earth behaves like a magnet.

120
00:05:01,106 --> 00:05:02,046
Well done!

121
00:05:02,843 --> 00:05:03,453
Look!

122
00:05:03,703 --> 00:05:06,943
My compass needle lines up with Basil's cones too.

123
00:05:07,043 --> 00:05:08,742
Is the needle a magnet?

124
00:05:08,762 --> 00:05:10,352
Find out in Part Two!

125
00:05:11,512 --> 00:05:12,613
Say it with us!

126
00:05:13,413 --> 00:05:14,163
Ready?

127
00:05:14,286 --> 00:05:14,946
One!

128
00:05:15,286 --> 00:05:15,986
two!

129
00:05:16,291 --> 00:05:17,466
Now you know!
